# fixedbugs, defect 2389, 2026-11-09.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header defining `#define t1 t2`, which turns the name of one
# temporary of the C this compiler writes into another's, was *internal
# error* at exit 2: clang's *redefinition of 't2'* stands at the real
# `t2`, its first note *previous definition is here*, and only its second
# the macro's, where the reader looked first.
#
# FIX: panel 214's R3 reads the first note under the error that expands a
# macro, wherever it stands (`cli/own_names.hero`, `met`), and the emitter's
# names of a body are among its forms, so the header is told at exit 1.

extern "fixedbugs-2389-a-header-s-macro-turning-a-temporary-into-another-is-told.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function plus(x: i64, y: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(plus(x: 40, y: 2))
